# ── Always ignored: churn and local state, never wanted in git ──

# Obsidian.
# .trash/ is where Obsidian moves deleted notes rather than removing them.
# Plugin data.json can hold API keys. workspace.json changes constantly.
.trash/
.obsidian/workspace*.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# Claude Code local settings and runtime logs.
# Logs append on every run and conflict on every pull.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/skills/**/*.log

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/


# ── Your decision: source documents in uploads/ ──
#
# uploads/ holds documents you were given rather than notes you wrote —
# performance reviews about named reports, HR material, past annual reviews.
#
# Versioning them is reasonable: it's your private repo and they're the
# context behind your notes. The one asymmetry worth thinking about is that
# a leak of your memory.md is your problem, while a leak of a review about
# a named report is that person's problem.
#
# Uncomment to keep them out of git entirely:
#
# uploads/**
# !uploads/**/
# !uploads/**/.gitkeep
